WEBVTT

00:00:00.015 --> 00:00:02.522
Easy Fables. Part 2.

00:00:02.522 --> 00:00:04.580
The Ant and the Grasshopper.

00:00:04.580 --> 00:00:09.125
All summer long, a grasshopper sat in the sun and sang.

00:00:09.125 --> 00:00:11.886
Near him, an ant was working hard.

00:00:11.886 --> 00:00:15.361
She carried food to her house, piece by piece.

00:00:15.361 --> 00:00:18.895
"Why do you work so hard?" asked the grasshopper.

00:00:18.895 --> 00:00:20.654
"Come and sing with me.

00:00:20.654 --> 00:00:22.981
There is lots of food everywhere."

00:00:22.981 --> 00:00:26.316
"I am saving food for the winter," said the ant.

00:00:26.316 --> 00:00:27.976
"You should do the same."

00:00:27.976 --> 00:00:33.027
"Winter is far away," said the grasshopper, and he went on singing.

00:00:33.027 --> 00:00:34.430
Then winter came.

00:00:34.430 --> 00:00:38.928
Snow covered the ground, and the grasshopper had nothing to eat.

00:00:38.928 --> 00:00:40.900
He was cold and hungry.

00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:43.942
He went to the ant's house and asked for food.

00:00:43.942 --> 00:00:46.999
"What did you do all summer?" asked the ant.

00:00:46.999 --> 00:00:49.578
"I sang," said the grasshopper.

00:00:49.578 --> 00:00:54.403
"Then now you can dance," said the ant, and she shut the door.

00:00:54.403 --> 00:00:57.657
Work today, and you will have what you need tomorrow.

00:00:57.657 --> 00:00:59.422
The Fox and the Crow.

00:00:59.422 --> 00:01:02.029
A crow found a big piece of cheese.

00:01:02.029 --> 00:01:04.542
She flew up into a tree to eat it.

00:01:04.542 --> 00:01:07.933
A fox saw her and wanted the cheese for himself.

00:01:07.933 --> 00:01:11.544
"Good morning, beautiful bird," said the fox.

00:01:11.544 --> 00:01:13.886
"What fine black feathers you have!

00:01:13.886 --> 00:01:15.363
What bright eyes!

00:01:15.363 --> 00:01:17.938
I am sure your voice is beautiful too.

00:01:17.938 --> 00:01:20.119
Please sing one song for me."

00:01:20.119 --> 00:01:22.229
The crow was very pleased.

00:01:22.229 --> 00:01:25.306
Nobody had ever said such nice things to her.

00:01:25.306 --> 00:01:27.431
She opened her mouth to sing.

00:01:27.431 --> 00:01:31.401
The cheese fell out, and the fox caught it at once.

00:01:31.401 --> 00:01:34.208
"Thank you," said the fox as he ate.

00:01:34.208 --> 00:01:35.769
"Your voice is fine.

00:01:35.769 --> 00:01:38.149
But you need to be a little more careful."

00:01:38.149 --> 00:01:41.337
Do not believe everyone who says nice things to you.

00:01:41.337 --> 00:01:43.249
The Dog and His Shadow.

00:01:43.249 --> 00:01:46.501
A dog was carrying a piece of meat in his mouth.

00:01:46.501 --> 00:01:48.660
He was taking it home to eat.

00:01:48.660 --> 00:01:52.859
On the way, he had to cross a small river on a bridge.

00:01:52.859 --> 00:01:54.894
He looked down into the water.

00:01:54.894 --> 00:01:58.384
There he saw another dog, with another piece of meat.

00:01:58.384 --> 00:02:01.340
He did not know that he was looking at himself.

00:02:01.340 --> 00:02:04.785
"That piece of meat is bigger than mine," he thought.

00:02:04.785 --> 00:02:06.128
"I want it too."

00:02:06.128 --> 00:02:09.297
He opened his mouth to take the other piece of meat.

00:02:09.297 --> 00:02:13.870
His own meat fell into the river and was carried away by the water.

00:02:13.870 --> 00:02:15.890
Now he had nothing at all.

00:02:15.890 --> 00:02:19.984
If you want too much, you may lose what you already have.

00:02:19.984 --> 00:02:21.998
The North Wind and the Sun.

00:02:21.998 --> 00:02:24.570
The north wind and the sun were talking.

00:02:24.570 --> 00:02:27.410
"I am stronger than you," said the wind.

00:02:27.410 --> 00:02:30.671
"No, I am stronger," said the sun.

00:02:30.671 --> 00:02:33.496
Just then a man came walking along the road.

00:02:33.496 --> 00:02:35.643
He was wearing a warm coat.

00:02:35.643 --> 00:02:40.265
"Let us see who can make that man take off his coat," said the sun.

00:02:40.265 --> 00:02:41.906
"You can try first."

00:02:41.906 --> 00:02:44.258
The wind blew as hard as he could.

00:02:44.258 --> 00:02:49.387
But the harder he blew, the more closely the man held his coat around him.

00:02:49.387 --> 00:02:51.376
At last the wind gave up.

00:02:51.376 --> 00:02:53.237
Then the sun came out.

00:02:53.237 --> 00:02:55.410
He shone warmly on the man.

00:02:55.410 --> 00:02:57.451
Soon the man felt hot.

00:02:57.451 --> 00:02:59.008
He opened his coat.

00:02:59.008 --> 00:03:02.171
Then he took it off and sat down under a tree.

00:03:02.171 --> 00:03:05.244
Being kind often works better than being hard.

00:03:05.244 --> 00:03:07.435
The Goose and the Golden Eggs.

00:03:08.050 --> 00:03:11.164
A farmer and his wife had a wonderful goose.

00:03:11.164 --> 00:03:15.749
Every morning she gave them one egg, and the egg was made of gold.

00:03:15.749 --> 00:03:19.289
They sold the eggs and soon they had a lot of money.

00:03:19.289 --> 00:03:20.727
But they wanted more.

00:03:20.727 --> 00:03:24.076
"One egg a day is too slow," said the farmer.

00:03:24.076 --> 00:03:27.167
"There must be a lot of gold inside that goose.

00:03:27.167 --> 00:03:30.277
Let us cut her open and take it all at once."

00:03:30.277 --> 00:03:33.161
So they killed the goose and cut her open.

00:03:33.161 --> 00:03:35.400
But there was no gold inside.

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:37.833
She was just like any other goose.

00:03:37.833 --> 00:03:41.112
Now they had no goose and no more golden eggs.

00:03:41.112 --> 00:03:44.791
People who want everything at once often end up with nothing.
